XFirst, can I assume we're talking about Nethack? If not, perhaps a
subset Xof the following will apply. I only play V2.2, the strategies
may vary Xfor V2.3 .
X
XThe game is played in stages, with different goals and strategies at
each Xstage. Here is a brief rundown:
X
X1. Getting Started - Escaping the Orcs
X
XYou must reach at least experience level 3 (25 or more HP) before
you go Xdown very far in the dungeon. I usually stay on Levels 1-2
until I reach Xthis point. I always leave the dog on Level 1 unless I
run into a bunch Xof Orcs on Level 2, in which case I use him to run
interference while I Xdash to the '>' down to Level 3. Orcs are the
most difficult monster Xyou have to deal with at this stage. You
should avoid prolonged fights Xwith them until your armor is 2 or
lower. When you are ready to take Xthem on, pick your battlefield
carefully. You should have a clear path Xto a staircase. Don't let
them circle and block your retreat. Get them Xto chase you down a
corridor where you can turn a corner and fight them Xone at a time
without taking darts from the Orcs in the rear. If you Xhave a 'hit
at a distance' wand, you may want to fire it at them down a Xstraight
hallway to take out several at once. If you find your hit points
Xgetting low, beat a hasty retreat to the stairs. You can always wait
on Xanother level to regenerate and come back to finish the fight
later. Once Xyou have the Orcs under control, you are ready for the
next stage. X
X2. Identifying Magic Items - Beating the killer bees
X
XDon't read any scrolls until you have more than you can carry. This
is Xusually around Level 7 or lower. Dump all your scrolls,
spellbooks and Xspare items by the '>', then go to lower levels and
bring back all the Xscrolls you find there. The idea is to get as
many scrolls as possible. XKeep going down until you run into
